{"repositoryId":333599546,"availability":"available","full":"kip-dili/kip","name":"kip","description":"A programming language in Turkish where grammatical case and mood are part of the type system.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Haskell","stars":880,"forks":21,"created":"2021-01-28T00:32:38Z","updated":"2026-09-26T02:27:37Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kip-dili.github.io","topics":["grammatical-cases","morphological-analysis","programming-language","turkish"],"demo":"https://kip-dili.github.io/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T21:03:52.742Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T21:03:52.742Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T21:03:52.742Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T20:33:40.008Z","stars":880,"forks":21},{"at":"2026-10-18T21:03:52.742Z","stars":880,"forks":21}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Kip (meaning \"grammatical mood\" in Turkish) is an experimental programming language that uses Turkish grammatical cases as part of its type system. It demonstrates how natural language morphology—specifically Turkish noun cases and vowel harmony—can be integrated into programming language design.","This is a research/educational project exploring the intersection of linguistics and type theory, not a production programming language.","There is also a tutorial in Turkish and a tutorial in English that explains how to write Kip programs."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kip-dili/kip/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b7477578d2d1da8c3129204dd9a26ef50fdef777e043b7a684efad44ddbfaf25","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T20:33:40.148Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T20:33:40.148Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Kip (meaning \"grammatical mood\" in Turkish) is an experimental programming language that uses Turkish grammatical cases as part of its type system. It demonstrates how natural language morphology—specifically Turkish noun cases and vowel harmony—can